    "['pim ipv6 sm', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols pim interface <interface-name> mode sparse', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols pim interface <interface-name> mode sparse', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols pim interface <interface-name> mode sparse\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, you would need to specify the interface name (e.g., `ge-1/0/0.0`) when applying the PIM configuration, unlike Huawei where it's configured directly under the interface. The equivalent Juniper command enables PIM Sparse Mode (SM) for IPv6 multicast on the specified interface.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols pim interface <interface-name> mode sparse'}]]": 1,
    "['pim ipv6 sm', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols pim interface all mode sparse', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols pim interface all mode sparse\\n##\\n\\nOr for more specific interface-based configuration (Juniper style):\\n\\n##\\nset protocols pim interface ge-1/0/0.0 mode sparse\\nset protocols pim interface ge-1/0/1.0 mode sparse\\nset protocols pim interface ge-1/0/2.0 mode sparse\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. \"sm\" (Sparse Mode) in Huawei translates to \"sparse\" mode in Juniper.\\n2. Juniper typically uses interface names with logical unit (e.g., ge-1/0/0.0).\\n3. The first example enables sparse mode globally on all interfaces, while the second specifies interfaces individually like the Huawei config.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols pim interface all mode sparse'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols pim interface ge-1/0/0.0 mode sparse', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols pim interface all mode sparse\\n##\\n\\nOr for more specific interface-based configuration (Juniper style):\\n\\n##\\nset protocols pim interface ge-1/0/0.0 mode sparse\\nset protocols pim interface ge-1/0/1.0 mode sparse\\nset protocols pim interface ge-1/0/2.0 mode sparse\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. \"sm\" (Sparse Mode) in Huawei translates to \"sparse\" mode in Juniper.\\n2. Juniper typically uses interface names with logical unit (e.g., ge-1/0/0.0).\\n3. The first example enables sparse mode globally on all interfaces, while the second specifies interfaces individually like the Huawei config.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols pim interface ge-1/0/0.0 mode sparse'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols pim interface ge-1/0/1.0 mode sparse', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols pim interface all mode sparse\\n##\\n\\nOr for more specific interface-based configuration (Juniper style):\\n\\n##\\nset protocols pim interface ge-1/0/0.0 mode sparse\\nset protocols pim interface ge-1/0/1.0 mode sparse\\nset protocols pim interface ge-1/0/2.0 mode sparse\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. \"sm\" (Sparse Mode) in Huawei translates to \"sparse\" mode in Juniper.\\n2. Juniper typically uses interface names with logical unit (e.g., ge-1/0/0.0).\\n3. The first example enables sparse mode globally on all interfaces, while the second specifies interfaces individually like the Huawei config.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols pim interface ge-1/0/1.0 mode sparse'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols pim interface ge-1/0/2.0 mode sparse', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols pim interface all mode sparse\\n##\\n\\nOr for more specific interface-based configuration (Juniper style):\\n\\n##\\nset protocols pim interface ge-1/0/0.0 mode sparse\\nset protocols pim interface ge-1/0/1.0 mode sparse\\nset protocols pim interface ge-1/0/2.0 mode sparse\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. \"sm\" (Sparse Mode) in Huawei translates to \"sparse\" mode in Juniper.\\n2. Juniper typically uses interface names with logical unit (e.g., ge-1/0/0.0).\\n3. The first example enables sparse mode globally on all interfaces, while the second specifies interfaces individually like the Huawei config.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols pim interface ge-1/0/2.0 mode sparse'}]]": 1,
